window.KIT_LOAD&&KIT_LOAD("m15",{"qb-ml-foundations":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Quick answers on splits, overfitting, regularisation, optimisation and training basics.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Data split, overfitting, regularisation, optimisation আর training-এর গোড়ার কথা, ছোট উত্তরে।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is overfitting and how do you spot it?","a":"The model memorises training data and fails on new data. Training loss keeps falling while validation loss stops improving or rises.","bn":"Model training data মুখস্থ করে নতুন data-য় ফেল করে; train loss কমে, validation loss থামে বা বাড়ে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why three splits (train, validation, test)?","a":"Train fits parameters, validation picks hyperparameters and stopping points, and test is touched once for an unbiased final estimate.","bn":"Train শেখায়, validation hyperparameter বাছে, test শেষে একবারই দেখা হয়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is data leakage? Give an example.","a":"Information from the test set reaching training, for example duplicates across splits or normalising on the whole dataset before splitting. It inflates scores.","bn":"Test-এর তথ্য training-এ ঢুকে পড়া, যেমন split-এর আগে পুরো data normalise করা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Bias vs variance in one sentence each.","a":"Bias is error from a model too simple to capture the pattern (underfit); variance is error from sensitivity to the particular training sample (overfit).","bn":"Bias = model খুব সরল তাই ধরতে পারে না; variance = training sample-এর প্রতি অতিসংবেদনশীল।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How does L2 regularisation differ from L1?","a":"L2 adds the squared weights to the loss and shrinks them smoothly; L1 adds absolute values and tends to push some weights exactly to zero (sparsity).","bn":"L2 weight ছোট করে; L1 কিছু weight শূন্য করে দেয়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does dropout do?","a":"It randomly zeroes activations during training so units can&#39;t co-adapt, acting like averaging many sub-networks. It is off at inference.","bn":"Training-এ কিছু unit এলোমেলো বন্ধ করে; inference-এ বন্ধ থাকে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is early stopping?","a":"Stop training when validation loss stops improving and keep the best checkpoint, which limits overfitting.","bn":"Validation loss-এর উন্নতি থামলে training থামাও, সেরা checkpoint রাখো।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why does gradient descent use a learning rate?","a":"It scales each step along the negative gradient. Too large and the loss diverges or oscillates; too small and training is slow or stuck.","bn":"প্রতিটা ধাপের আকার ঠিক করে; বেশি হলে ছিটকে যায়, কম হলে ধীর।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"SGD vs Adam?","a":"SGD uses one global step size (often with momentum); Adam keeps running averages of the gradient and its square to adapt a step size per parameter. Adam converges fast with little tuning; SGD can generalise well.","bn":"Adam প্রতি parameter-এর step নিজে মানিয়ে নেয়; SGD সরল।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is the vanishing gradient problem?","a":"In deep networks gradients shrink as they are multiplied backwards through layers, so early layers barely learn. Fixes: ReLU-type activations, residual connections, normalisation, good initialisation.","bn":"গভীর network-এ gradient পিছনে যেতে যেতে ছোট হয়ে যায়; residual connection আর normalisation সাহায্য করে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does batch normalisation or layer norm do?","a":"It normalises activations to stable mean and variance, which steadies training. Transformers use layer norm because it doesn&#39;t depend on batch size.","bn":"Activation স্থিতিশীল রাখে; Transformer-এ layer norm।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why shuffle the training data?","a":"So each batch is a representative sample and the model doesn&#39;t learn the data order or get biased gradients from sorted classes.","bn":"যাতে প্রতিটা batch প্রতিনিধিত্বমূলক হয়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is cross-validation and when would you use it?","a":"Splitting data into k folds and rotating which fold validates. It gives a steadier estimate on small datasets; for huge LLM training it is too expensive.","bn":"k ভাগে ভাগ করে ঘুরিয়ে validate; ছোট dataset-এ কাজের।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is class imbalance and what can you do?","a":"One class is rare. Use better metrics (precision, recall, PR-AUC), resampling, class weights or threshold tuning, not accuracy alone.","bn":"একটা class বিরল; accuracy না, precision-recall দেখো, weight বা resampling দাও।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is the difference between a parameter and a hyperparameter?","a":"Parameters are learned by training (weights); hyperparameters are set before training (learning rate, batch size, LoRA rank).","bn":"Parameter training-এ শেখা হয়; hyperparameter আগে থেকে ঠিক করা।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is weight decay and how does AdamW treat it?","a":"Weight decay shrinks weights each step. AdamW applies it directly to the weights, decoupled from the adaptive gradient step, which is not the same as adding L2 to the loss under Adam.","bn":"AdamW weight decay আলাদা ভাবে প্রয়োগ করে, loss-এ L2 যোগ করার মতো না।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Why do we clip gradients?","a":"To cap exploding gradients so one bad batch can&#39;t blow up the weights; common in transformer training.","bn":"বড় gradient এক ধাক্কায় weight নষ্ট করা ঠেকাতে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is mixed precision training?","a":"Computing in 16-bit (bf16/fp16) with some values kept in fp32 to save memory and time. bf16 has fp32&#39;s range, so it needs no loss scaling.","bn":"16-bit-এ হিসাব, কিছু fp32-এ; bf16-এর range fp32-এর মতো।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is gradient accumulation?","a":"Summing gradients over several small batches before one optimiser step, to mimic a bigger batch when memory is limited. I used batch 1 × 16 accumulation steps.","bn":"ছোট batch-এর gradient জমিয়ে একবার update; memory কম হলে বড় batch-এর মতো।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Epoch, step and batch: what&#39;s the difference?","a":"A batch is a group of examples; a step is one optimiser update; an epoch is one pass over the whole dataset.","bn":"Batch = একদল উদাহরণ; step = একবার update; epoch = পুরো data একবার।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is double descent?","a":"Test error can fall, rise near the point where the model just fits the data, then fall again as the model grows much larger.","bn":"Model বড় করলে test error কমে, বাড়ে, আবার কমে।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is label smoothing?","a":"Replace one-hot targets with slightly softened ones (for example 0.9 and 0.1 spread), which reduces overconfidence.","bn":"One-hot target একটু নরম করা, যাতে model অতি-আত্মবিশ্বাসী না হয়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How do you debug a model whose loss doesn&#39;t go down?","a":"Overfit one tiny batch first, check the learning rate, the labels and input alignment, the gradient norm and that parameters are actually trainable.","bn":"আগে ছোট batch overfit করাও, label, learning rate, grad_norm আর trainable parameter দেখো।","level":"medium","trick":false}]},"qb-losses-metrics":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Cross-entropy, KL, BCE, precision-recall, ROC, calibration and the metrics people confuse.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Cross-entropy, KL, BCE, precision-recall, ROC, calibration আর যেসব metric গুলিয়ে ফেলা হয়।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"What does cross-entropy measure?","a":"The average number of nats (or bits) needed to encode true labels using the model&#39;s predicted distribution. With one-hot labels it is the negative log-probability of the correct class.","bn":"Model-এর distribution দিয়ে সঠিক label encode করতে গড়ে কত লাগে; one-hot হলে সঠিক class-এর −log p।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How are cross-entropy, entropy and KL related?","a":"H(p, q) = H(p) + KL(p ‖ q). Cross-entropy is entropy plus the extra cost of using q instead of p.","bn":"Cross-entropy = entropy + KL।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Is KL divergence symmetric? Is it a distance?","a":"No to both. KL(p ‖ q) ≠ KL(q ‖ p) and it violates the triangle inequality. JS divergence is a symmetric smoothed version.","bn":"না; দুই দিকের মান আলাদা, আর এটা আসল distance না।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"When do you use BCE and when softmax cross-entropy?","a":"BCE for independent binary or multi-label outputs (sigmoid); softmax cross-entropy for exactly one class out of many.","bn":"একাধিক সঠিক হতে পারলে BCE; একটাই সঠিক হলে softmax CE।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"MSE vs MAE?","a":"MSE squares errors, so it punishes outliers heavily and is smooth; MAE is robust to outliers but has a constant gradient. Huber mixes both.","bn":"MSE outlier-কে বেশি শাস্তি দেয়; MAE outlier-সহনশীল।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is focal loss for?","a":"It down-weights easy examples so training focuses on hard ones, useful for heavy class imbalance such as object detection.","bn":"সহজ উদাহরণের weight কমিয়ে কঠিনগুলোতে মনোযোগ দেয়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Define precision and recall with an example.","a":"Precision = TP/(TP+FP): of what I flagged, how much was right. Recall = TP/(TP+FN): of what was there, how much I found. A spam filter that flags 10 emails with 8 spam and misses 4 has precision 0.8 and recall about 0.67.","bn":"Precision = যা ধরেছি তার কতটা ঠিক; recall = যা ছিল তার কতটা ধরেছি।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why F1 and not the average of precision and recall?","a":"F1 is the harmonic mean, so it is low if either is low and can&#39;t hide a bad one.","bn":"Harmonic mean, একটা খারাপ হলে F1-ও খারাপ।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Macro vs micro averaging?","a":"Macro averages the metric per class equally; micro pools all counts first, so large classes dominate.","bn":"Macro = প্রতি class সমান; micro = সব count একসাথে, বড় class বেশি প্রভাব ফেলে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does ROC-AUC mean?","a":"The probability that a random positive is scored above a random negative. 0.5 is chance, 1.0 is perfect.","bn":"একটা এলোমেলো positive, negative-এর চেয়ে বেশি স্কোর পাওয়ার সম্ভাবনা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"When is PR-AUC better than ROC-AUC?","a":"With heavy class imbalance, because ROC-AUC can look good when the huge negative class makes the false-positive rate tiny.","bn":"Class imbalance বেশি হলে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is calibration?","a":"Predicted probabilities match observed frequencies: among predictions of 0.8, about 80% are correct. Measured by ECE or Brier score.","bn":"৮০% বললে সত্যিই ~৮০% ঠিক হওয়া; ECE বা Brier score।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Define perplexity.","a":"exp of the mean per-token cross-entropy (in nats). It is the model&#39;s effective branching factor; lower is better.","bn":"Token-প্রতি গড় cross-entropy-র exp; কম মানে ভালো।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Can you compare perplexity across models with different tokenizers?","a":"Not directly: perplexity is per token, and different tokenizers split text differently. Compare bits per character or per byte instead.","bn":"সরাসরি না, tokenizer আলাদা হলে token ভিন্ন; bits per character দেখো।","level":"hard","trick":true},{"q":"What does BLEU measure?","a":"Modified n-gram precision (n = 1 to 4) combined geometrically, times a brevity penalty. Precision-oriented, built for translation.","bn":"n-gram precision আর brevity penalty; অনুবাদের জন্য।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does ROUGE-L measure?","a":"An F-measure based on the longest common subsequence between candidate and reference.","bn":"Longest common subsequence-ভিত্তিক F-measure।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"BLEU vs ROUGE in one line.","a":"BLEU is precision-oriented (is what I wrote in the reference?); ROUGE is recall-oriented (did I cover the reference?), though F1 versions are common.","bn":"BLEU precision-ঘেঁষা; ROUGE recall-ঘেঁষা।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does BERTScore do that ROUGE can&#39;t?","a":"It matches tokens by contextual embedding similarity, so paraphrases score well even with no word overlap.","bn":"শব্দ না মিললেও অর্থ মিললে নম্বর দেয়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why can ROUGE mislead for legal or medical text?","a":"One changed token (Section 302 vs 304) barely changes the score but changes the meaning completely, and style copying is rewarded.","bn":"একটা সংখ্যা বদলালে অর্থ পুরো বদলায়, কিন্তু ROUGE প্রায় একই।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is MRR?","a":"Mean reciprocal rank: the average of 1/rank of the first relevant result per query.","bn":"প্রথম সঠিক ফলের 1/rank-এর গড়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Recall@k vs precision@k?","a":"Recall@k is the share of all relevant items found in the top k; precision@k is the share of the top k that are relevant.","bn":"Recall@k = সব সঠিকের কতটা top-k-তে; precision@k = top-k-র কতটা সঠিক।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does nDCG add over precision@k?","a":"It rewards putting relevant items higher and handles graded relevance.","bn":"সঠিক ফল উপরে থাকলে বেশি নম্বর।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is Cohen&#39;s kappa?","a":"Agreement between two raters corrected for the agreement expected by chance.","bn":"দুই rater-এর মিল, কাকতালীয় মিল বাদ দিয়ে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is the unbiased pass@k?","a":"1 − C(n−c, k)/C(n, k) with n samples and c correct, the chance at least one of k samples passes.","bn":"n নমুনার c সঠিক হলে k-তে অন্তত একটা পাস হওয়ার সম্ভাবনা।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Why is accuracy a bad metric for a 1%-positive problem?","a":"Predicting all negative gives 99% accuracy while finding nothing.","bn":"সব negative বললেই 99%।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How do you pick a classification threshold?","a":"From the cost of each error type: sweep the threshold on validation data and pick the point on the precision-recall curve that fits the use case.","bn":"কোন ভুলের খরচ বেশি তা দেখে PR curve থেকে বাছো।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is the T² factor in the Hinton KD loss?","a":"Soft-target gradients scale like 1/T², so multiplying the KL by T² keeps its size comparable to the hard-label loss as T changes.","bn":"T বাড়ালে soft loss-এর gradient ছোট হয়, T² দিয়ে গুণ করলে balance থাকে।","level":"medium","trick":false}]},"qb-llm-eval":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Benchmarks, LLM-as-judge, contamination, human evaluation and statistics for generative models.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Benchmark, LLM-as-judge, contamination, মানুষের মূল্যায়ন আর generative model-এর পরিসংখ্যান।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why is evaluating generation harder than classification?","a":"There are many valid outputs, so exact match fails; you need overlap metrics, embedding metrics, judges or humans, each with biases.","bn":"অনেক উত্তরই ঠিক হতে পারে, তাই এক সঠিক উত্তরের সাথে মেলানো যায় না।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is LLM-as-a-judge?","a":"Using a strong model to score or compare outputs against a rubric. It&#39;s cheap and scalable but has biases and must be calibrated against humans.","bn":"শক্তিশালী model দিয়ে নম্বর দেওয়া; মানুষের সাথে মিলিয়ে নিতে হয়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Name three judge biases.","a":"Position bias (prefers the first answer), verbosity bias (prefers longer answers) and self-preference (prefers its own family&#39;s style).","bn":"অবস্থান, দৈর্ঘ্য আর নিজের ধাঁচের প্রতি পক্ষপাত।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How do you reduce position bias in pairwise judging?","a":"Run each comparison twice with the order swapped and count only consistent verdicts, or randomise the order.","bn":"ক্রম বদলে দুবার চালাও।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is benchmark contamination?","a":"Test items leaked into training data, so scores overstate ability. Check n-gram overlap, use fresh or private test sets.","bn":"Test প্রশ্ন training data-য় ছিল, তাই নম্বর ফুলে যায়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does MMLU test, and what&#39;s its weakness?","a":"Multi-subject multiple-choice knowledge. It is saturated for frontier models, sensitive to prompt format and partly contaminated.","bn":"বহু বিষয়ের MCQ জ্ঞান; frontier model-এর জন্য সীমা ছুঁয়েছে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How would you evaluate a distilled student against its teacher?","a":"Same prompts and decoding on a held-out set; compare task metrics, a calibrated judge, human ratings on a sample, plus size, latency and cost, and report confidence intervals.","bn":"একই prompt আর decoding-এ held-out set, metric, judge, মানুষের নম্বর, size-latency।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is faithfulness in RAG evaluation?","a":"Whether every claim in the answer is supported by the retrieved context.","bn":"উত্তরের প্রতিটা দাবি retrieve করা context-এ আছে কি না।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Faithfulness vs answer relevance?","a":"Faithfulness is groundedness in the context; relevance is whether the answer addresses the question. An answer can be faithful but off-topic, or relevant but invented.","bn":"Faithfulness = context-এ ভিত্তি; relevance = প্রশ্নের উত্তর কি না।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How many test examples do you need to claim model A beats B?","a":"Enough that the confidence interval of the difference excludes zero. With 50 examples, differences of a few points are usually noise; use paired tests or bootstrap.","bn":"৫০টায় ছোট তফাত প্রায়ই noise; bootstrap বা paired test।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is human evaluation&#39;s main problem?","a":"Cost and inconsistency; use clear rubrics, several raters and report agreement such as kappa.","bn":"খরচ আর রায়ের অমিল; rubric আর একাধিক rater।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does a bimodal LLM-judge score distribution tell you?","a":"The judge acts like a pass/fail classifier on a 1–5 scale, so the average hides it. Mine gave 25 ones and 15 fives out of 50.","bn":"Judge আসলে pass/fail করছে, গড় ভুল ধারণা দেয়।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Which metrics for a coding model?","a":"Unit-test based pass@k, not text overlap.","bn":"Unit test দিয়ে pass@k।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is exact match and token F1 used for?","a":"Extractive QA: exact match requires the same string; token F1 gives partial credit by overlap.","bn":"Extractive QA-তে; F1 আংশিক নম্বর দেয়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What should you report besides accuracy for a distilled model?","a":"Parameter count, memory, latency or tokens per second, energy or cost, and the teacher&#39;s score for reference.","bn":"Size, latency, খরচ আর teacher-এর নম্বর।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is win rate and how is it computed?","a":"The share of pairwise comparisons one model wins, judged by humans or a judge; Elo or Bradley-Terry turn many pairs into a ranking.","bn":"জোড়ায় জোড়ায় তুলনায় কতবার জেতে।","level":"medium","trick":false}]},"qb-transformers":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Attention, tokenisation, positional encoding, KV cache and decoding.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Attention কীভাবে কাজ করে, লেখা কীভাবে token হয়, position কীভাবে বোঝা যায়, আর KV cache ও decoding-এর ছোট উত্তর।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"Write the attention formula and say why we divide by √d.","a":"softmax(QKᵀ/√d_k)V. Without scaling, dot products grow with dimension and push softmax into saturation with tiny gradients.","bn":"softmax(QKᵀ/√d)V; ভাগ না করলে softmax সংকুচিত হয়ে gradient ছোট হয়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is self-attention in plain words?","a":"Each token builds its new representation as a weighted mix of all tokens&#39; values, with weights from how well its query matches their keys.","bn":"প্রতিটা token অন্য সব token-এর value-র weighted মিশ্রণ নেয়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why multiple heads?","a":"Different heads can attend to different relations (syntax, position, coreference) in parallel subspaces.","bn":"আলাদা head আলাদা সম্পর্ক দেখে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why do transformers need positional information?","a":"Attention is permutation-invariant, so order has to be injected: sinusoidal, learned or rotary (RoPE) embeddings.","bn":"Attention ক্রম বোঝে না, তাই position যোগ করতে হয়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does the causal mask do?","a":"Blocks attention to future positions so a decoder predicts the next token only from earlier ones.","bn":"ভবিষ্যৎ token দেখা বন্ধ করে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Encoder-only, decoder-only, encoder-decoder: an example of each?","a":"BERT (and e5) is encoder-only; GPT, Llama and Gemma are decoder-only; T5 is encoder-decoder.","bn":"BERT/e5 encoder; GPT/Gemma decoder; T5 encoder-decoder।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is the KV cache?","a":"Stored keys and values of past tokens, so each new token only computes its own K and V instead of recomputing the whole sequence. Memory grows with batch × length × layers.","bn":"আগের token-এর K-V জমা রাখা; নতুন token-এর জন্য শুধু নতুন অংশ হিসাব হয়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why is attention O(n²)?","a":"Every token scores every other token, so the score matrix is n × n in compute and memory.","bn":"প্রতিটা token প্রতিটার সাথে মেলে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does FlashAttention change?","a":"It computes exact attention in tiles in fast on-chip memory without materialising the n × n matrix, cutting memory traffic and memory use.","bn":"পুরো n×n matrix বানায় না, ছোট টুকরোয় হিসাব করে।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"MHA vs MQA vs GQA?","a":"MHA has separate K/V per head; MQA shares one K/V across heads; GQA shares K/V across groups of heads, a middle ground that shrinks the KV cache with little quality loss.","bn":"GQA-তে head-এর দলের মধ্যে K-V ভাগ হয়, KV cache ছোট হয়।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is BPE tokenisation?","a":"Start from characters or bytes and repeatedly merge the most frequent pairs into a vocabulary of subword tokens.","bn":"সবচেয়ে বেশি আসা জোড়া মিলিয়ে subword বানায়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why do some tokenisers need so many tokens for Bangla?","a":"Their vocabulary was learned mostly from English text, so Bengali script falls back to small or byte pieces. Llama 3.1 needs about 8 tokens per Bangla word versus Gemma 2&#39;s about 3.7.","bn":"Vocabulary English-প্রধান, তাই Bengali ভেঙে যায়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Greedy vs sampling vs beam search?","a":"Greedy takes the top token each step; sampling draws from the distribution (with T, top-k, top-p); beam search keeps the best several sequences. Greedy and beam are deterministic.","bn":"Greedy সবসময় সেরা; sampling বিভিন্নতা আনে; beam কয়েকটা পথ রাখে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does temperature do at decoding?","a":"It divides logits before softmax: lower is more deterministic, higher more random. It is a different knob from distillation temperature.","bn":"কম হলে নিশ্চিত, বেশি হলে এলোমেলো।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is a Mixture of Experts?","a":"A layer with many expert networks where a router activates only a few per token, so total parameters are large but active parameters (and compute) are small.","bn":"অনেক expert, প্রতি token-এ কয়েকটা চালু; মোট parameter বেশি, কাজ কম।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is the training compute rule of thumb?","a":"About 6·N·D FLOPs for N parameters and D tokens; inference is about 2·N FLOPs per token.","bn":"Training ≈ 6·N·D; inference ≈ 2·N প্রতি token।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does Chinchilla say?","a":"For compute-optimal training use about 20 tokens per parameter, so many earlier models were undertrained.","bn":"প্রতি parameter-এ ~20 token।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is speculative decoding?","a":"A small draft model proposes several tokens and the large model verifies them in one pass, giving the large model&#39;s output distribution faster.","bn":"ছোট model কয়েকটা token প্রস্তাব করে, বড় model একবারে যাচাই করে।","level":"hard","trick":false}]},"qb-lifecycle-peft-compression":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Pretraining to RLHF/DPO, LoRA and QLoRA, quantisation, pruning and memory maths.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Pretraining থেকে RLHF/DPO, LoRA-QLoRA, quantisation, pruning আর memory-র হিসাব।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"What are the stages of building an assistant LLM?","a":"Pretraining on huge text, supervised instruction tuning (SFT), then preference alignment (RLHF, DPO or similar).","bn":"Pretraining, SFT, তারপর preference alignment।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"SFT vs RLHF vs DPO?","a":"SFT imitates demonstrations; RLHF trains a reward model and optimises against it with RL; DPO optimises the policy directly on preference pairs without a separate reward model or RL loop.","bn":"SFT অনুকরণ; RLHF reward model + RL; DPO সরাসরি preference জোড়া থেকে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why does LoRA work?","a":"Fine-tuning updates tend to have low intrinsic rank, so a low-rank update BA captures most of the change with far fewer parameters.","bn":"Fine-tuning-এর পরিবর্তন সাধারণত low-rank।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How many trainable parameters does LoRA add for a d × k matrix with rank r?","a":"r(d + k).","bn":"r(d + k)।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why initialise B to zero in LoRA?","a":"So the update starts at zero and the model begins exactly as the base model.","bn":"শুরুতে model অপরিবর্তিত থাকে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does the LoRA α do?","a":"It scales the update by α/r. Changing r without α changes the effective update size.","bn":"আপডেটকে α/r দিয়ে scale করে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is QLoRA?","a":"LoRA on a frozen base model quantised to 4-bit NF4, with double quantisation and paged optimisers. Adapters train in 16-bit and gradients flow through the frozen 4-bit weights.","bn":"4-bit frozen base-এর উপর LoRA।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Is QLoRA the same as quantising the adapters?","a":"No. It quantises the frozen base; the adapters stay in 16-bit.","bn":"না; base quantise হয়, adapter নয়।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"What is NF4?","a":"A 4-bit data type whose levels fit normally distributed weights, giving less error than uniform 4-bit.","bn":"Normal distribution-এর জন্য বানানো 4-bit type।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"PTQ vs QAT?","a":"Post-training quantisation converts a trained model with little or no training; quantisation-aware training simulates quantisation during training for better accuracy at low bits.","bn":"PTQ training-এর পরে; QAT training-এর সময়েই।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Memory for a 7B model in fp16, int8, int4?","a":"About 14 GB, 7 GB and 3.5 GB for weights only (2, 1 and 0.5 bytes per parameter).","bn":"~14, 7, 3.5 GB।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Full fine-tuning memory per parameter with AdamW in mixed precision?","a":"Roughly 16 bytes per parameter (weights, gradients, optimiser states) plus activations.","bn":"প্রায় 16 byte প্রতি parameter।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is gradient checkpointing?","a":"Don&#39;t store all activations; recompute some in the backward pass, trading about a third more compute for much lower memory.","bn":"কিছু activation আবার হিসাব করে memory বাঁচায়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is catastrophic forgetting?","a":"Fine-tuning on a narrow task overwrites earlier abilities. LoRA, mixing in old data and low learning rates reduce it.","bn":"নতুন কাজ শিখতে গিয়ে পুরনো ক্ষমতা হারানো।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is pruning?","a":"Removing weights, neurons, heads or layers that matter least. Unstructured pruning gives sparsity that needs special hardware; structured pruning gives truly smaller dense models.","bn":"কম দরকারি অংশ বাদ দেওয়া।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is GGUF?","a":"The llama.cpp model file format that stores weights (often quantised, such as Q4_K_M) and metadata for CPU and mobile inference.","bn":"llama.cpp-এর model file format।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is Q4_K_M?","a":"A mixed 4-bit K-quant: most weights at about 4 bits, sensitive tensors at higher precision; about 5 bits per weight overall. My 2B model became 1.6 GB.","bn":"মিশ্র 4-bit; আমার 2B model 1.6 GB হয়েছে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why merge the adapter before quantising?","a":"Merging B·A into W in 16-bit is exact; merging into already-quantised weights corrupts the arithmetic.","bn":"আগে merge, তারপর quantise।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does continuous batching do?","a":"A serving engine adds new requests to the running batch as others finish instead of waiting for the whole batch, raising GPU utilisation.","bn":"নতুন request চলমান batch-এ ঢোকে।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is model merging?","a":"Combining weights of several fine-tuned models (averaging or task arithmetic) into one without more training.","bn":"কয়েকটা model-এর weight মিলিয়ে একটা।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Distillation vs quantisation vs pruning?","a":"Distillation trains a smaller model to imitate a bigger one; quantisation lowers precision per weight; pruning removes weights. They combine.","bn":"Distillation = ছোট model শেখানো; quantisation = precision কমানো; pruning = অংশ বাদ।","level":"easy","trick":false}]},"qb-distillation":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>The core of the interview: soft targets, temperature, KL direction, SeqKD, on-policy, top-k, tokenizers, licences and failure modes.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Interview-এর মূল অংশ: soft target, temperature, KL-এর দিক, SeqKD, on-policy, top-k, tokenizer, licence আর ব্যর্থতার কারণ।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"Define knowledge distillation in one sentence.","a":"Training a smaller student to imitate a larger teacher, usually from the teacher&#39;s output distributions or generated outputs rather than only hard labels.","bn":"ছোট student-কে বড় teacher-এর output নকল করতে শেখানো।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why are soft targets more informative than hard labels?","a":"They carry relative probabilities of wrong classes (dark knowledge), which tell the student which mistakes are close.","bn":"ভুল উত্তরগুলোর মধ্যে কোনটা কাছাকাছি তা জানায়।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is dark knowledge?","a":"The information in the small probabilities the teacher gives to incorrect outputs, such as a truck being a bit like a car and nothing like a carrot.","bn":"ভুল উত্তরের ছোট probability-র মধ্যে থাকা তথ্য।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Write the Hinton KD loss.","a":"L = α·CE(y, p_s) + (1−α)·T²·KL(p_t^T ‖ p_s^T), with p^T = softmax(z/T). Some papers weight the KD term with α instead.","bn":"α·CE + (1−α)·T²·KL(teacher ‖ student), দুটোই T-তে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does temperature do in KD?","a":"It softens both distributions so the small probabilities become visible and the student can learn from them.","bn":"Distribution নরম করে ছোট probability দৃশ্যমান করে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Is the student deployed at the distillation temperature?","a":"No, T is only used inside the training loss; the student runs at T = 1.","bn":"না; deploy-এ T = 1।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Is the teacher updated during standard KD?","a":"No, it is frozen. Only mutual learning and online distillation update both.","bn":"না, frozen।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Forward vs reverse KL in distillation?","a":"Forward KL(p_t ‖ q_s) is mode-covering, spreading student mass over all teacher modes; reverse KL(q_s ‖ p_t) is mode-seeking, committing to high-probability teacher modes (MiniLLM). Standard word-level KD uses forward KL.","bn":"Forward = সব mode ঢাকে; reverse = প্রধান mode ধরে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why might reverse KL suit text generation?","a":"A small student can&#39;t cover every teacher mode, and covering them puts mass on low-quality text; seeking the main modes gives more reliable generations.","bn":"ছোট student সব mode ধরতে পারে না; প্রধান mode ধরা ভালো।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Word-level KD vs sequence-level KD?","a":"Word-level matches the teacher&#39;s per-token distribution on given prefixes; sequence-level (SeqKD, Kim &amp; Rush 2016) trains the student with ordinary CE on sequences the teacher generated.","bn":"Word-level প্রতি token-এর distribution; SeqKD teacher-এর বানানো পুরো লেখা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is on-policy distillation?","a":"The student generates sequences, the teacher scores or corrects them, and the student learns on its own prefixes. It fixes exposure bias (GKD, MiniLLM).","bn":"Student নিজে লেখে, teacher নম্বর দেয়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is exposure bias?","a":"Training on gold or teacher prefixes but generating from its own prefixes at test time, so errors compound in situations never seen in training.","bn":"Training-এ সঠিক prefix, test-এ নিজের prefix।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is GKD?","a":"Generalised KD (Agarwal et al., ICLR 2024): train on student-generated sequences scored by the teacher with a generalised JSD, mixing on-policy and fixed data via <code>lmbda</code>, interpolating forward and reverse KL via <code>beta</code>.","bn":"Student-এর নিজের লেখার উপর teacher-এর মূল্যায়ন।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Why store only the top-k teacher logits?","a":"The full vocabulary distribution is huge (256K entries per token), but top-k covers most of the probability mass. My top-50 covered about 95%.","bn":"পুরো vocabulary রাখা অসম্ভব; top-k বেশিরভাগ mass ধরে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What bias does top-k truncation add?","a":"The tail mass is ignored, so the target is biased, even after renormalising. Remedies: a tail bucket, sampled logits, or reporting it as a limitation.","bn":"বাকি অংশের তথ্য হারায়, bias থাকে।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Why must teacher and student share a tokenizer for logit KD?","a":"Token-level KL compares distributions over the same vocabulary; different ids mean different tokens. Otherwise use sequence-level or cross-tokenizer KD.","bn":"একই vocabulary না হলে KL অর্থহীন।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is the capacity gap?","a":"A teacher far larger than the student can teach worse than a medium teacher because the student can&#39;t represent the teacher&#39;s function. Use a teacher assistant or an intermediate size.","bn":"Teacher অনেক বড় হলে student ধরতে পারে না।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Can a student outperform its teacher?","a":"Yes, in some cases: born-again networks with the same size, noisy students, or when the student gets extra data or a filter on the teacher&#39;s outputs.","bn":"কিছু ক্ষেত্রে হ্যাঁ।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is feature (hint) distillation?","a":"Matching intermediate representations, not just outputs, for example FitNets with a projection layer.","bn":"মাঝের layer-এর feature মেলানো।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is DistilBERT?","a":"A 6-layer BERT distilled from BERT-base (40% smaller, 60% faster, about 97% of the performance) using soft targets, cosine embedding and MLM losses.","bn":"BERT-এর ছোট সংস্করণ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is &quot;distilling step by step&quot;?","a":"Training the student on the teacher&#39;s rationales as well as labels, so small models need less data and can beat larger ones on some tasks.","bn":"Teacher-এর যুক্তি সহ শেখানো।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is Orca-style explanation tuning?","a":"Training a student on a strong teacher&#39;s step-by-step explanations in response to system prompts, not just final answers.","bn":"ধাপে ধাপে ব্যাখ্যা সহ শেখানো।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is black-box distillation?","a":"Distilling only from the teacher&#39;s text outputs (API access), with no logits; it&#39;s SeqKD or synthetic data training.","bn":"শুধু teacher-এর লেখা, logit নেই।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"White-box vs black-box: which is better?","a":"White-box gives richer signal (full distributions) but needs open weights; black-box works with any API but loses the dark knowledge.","bn":"White-box-এ বেশি তথ্য, কিন্তু open weight লাগে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is the teacher-fingerprinting risk?","a":"Students distilled from a model can inherit identifiable traits, which can show that a provider&#39;s outputs were used, relevant to terms of service.","bn":"Student-এ teacher-এর ছাপ থেকে যায়।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What are the licence risks of distillation?","a":"Some model terms forbid using outputs to train competing models, and some licences make derivatives inherit restrictions. Check the teacher&#39;s terms and prefer open licences such as Apache 2.0 or MIT.","bn":"কিছু licence-এ output দিয়ে প্রতিদ্বন্দ্বী model train নিষেধ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Which teachers would you pick today and why?","a":"Open-weight models with permissive licences and logit access, in the same tokenizer family as the student, such as a Qwen3 teacher for Qwen3 students. I&#39;d verify the licence first.","bn":"Open, permissive licence, একই tokenizer-এর teacher।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What&#39;s the difference between KD and fine-tuning?","a":"Fine-tuning learns from labelled data; KD learns from another model&#39;s outputs, which may be richer than labels. They are often combined.","bn":"Fine-tuning label থেকে; KD আরেক model-এর output থেকে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why does KD work at all?","a":"Soft targets carry more bits per example, act as a regulariser, and give the student an easier function to fit than raw labels.","bn":"প্রতি উদাহরণে বেশি তথ্য আর regularisation।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is multi-teacher distillation?","a":"Combining several teachers&#39; outputs (average, weighted or routed by domain), to merge strengths.","bn":"একাধিক teacher-এর মিলিত সংকেত।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is data-free distillation?","a":"Distilling without the original training data, by using synthetic inputs generated from the teacher.","bn":"মূল data ছাড়া।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"How do you pick α and T?","a":"Tune on validation: typical T is 1 to 5 (I used 4.0 on top-50), and α trades the hard-label signal against the soft signal; I found 0.4 KL weight best over 0.3 and 0.5.","bn":"Validation-এ tune; আমার KL weight 0.4 সেরা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is a quality gate in synthetic data pipelines?","a":"A filter that removes bad teacher outputs (too short, evasive, wrong format, duplicates). Mine kept 9,429 of 14,514.","bn":"খারাপ teacher উত্তর ছাঁটাই করা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What can a quality gate do wrong?","a":"Remove a whole behaviour. Mine deleted all abstentions, so the student never learned to say the context doesn&#39;t cover a question.","bn":"একটা পুরো আচরণই মুছে ফেলতে পারে।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is rejection sampling in distillation data?","a":"Generate several teacher outputs and keep only those that pass a verifier or score threshold.","bn":"কয়েকটা বানিয়ে যেগুলো পাস করে রাখা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why de-duplicate and decontaminate the data?","a":"Duplicates overweight some patterns and cause memorisation; contamination with test items inflates scores.","bn":"পুনরাবৃত্তি আর test leakage ঠেকাতে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is cross-tokenizer distillation?","a":"Methods that align different vocabularies (for example by mapping tokens or comparing sorted probability profiles) so a student can learn from a teacher with a different tokenizer.","bn":"আলাদা tokenizer-এর মধ্যে সংযোগ।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is the cost structure of distillation?","a":"Teacher inference for data (about 2N FLOPs per token), student training (6ND), and evaluation; paid once, and amortised across many deployments.","bn":"Teacher-এর data তৈরি, student training, মূল্যায়ন।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"When is distillation not worth it?","a":"Low volume, a task that changes every week, no good eval set, or a need for capabilities the student can&#39;t reach.","bn":"কম ব্যবহার, ঘন ঘন বদলানো কাজ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How is Gemma 3 itself trained?","a":"Its pretraining uses knowledge distillation from a larger teacher, storing 256 sampled logits per token per the Gemma 3 report.","bn":"Gemma 3 নিজেই distillation দিয়ে train হয়েছে।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What does DeepSeek-R1-Distill do?","a":"It fine-tunes smaller open models (Qwen, Llama bases) on about 800k samples generated by R1: sequence-level distillation of reasoning.","bn":"R1-এর বানানো উত্তরে ছোট model fine-tune।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is a draft model and how can distillation help it?","a":"A small model used in speculative decoding; distilling it from the target model raises its acceptance rate.","bn":"Speculative decoding-এর ছোট model।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Name three reasons a student underperforms.","a":"Train-eval format mismatch, capacity gap or bad teacher data, and loss set-up bugs such as applying T twice or misaligned targets.","bn":"Format অমিল, ক্ষমতার ফাঁক, loss-এর ভুল।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is mutual learning?","a":"Two or more students train together, each also learning from the others&#39; predictions, without a pre-trained teacher.","bn":"কয়েকটা student একে অপরকে শেখায়।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What does &quot;student beats teacher&quot; usually depend on?","a":"Task specialisation, filtering of teacher outputs, and extra signals such as retrieval or verification the teacher didn&#39;t use in training.","bn":"নির্দিষ্ট কাজ, ছাঁটাই, বাড়তি সংকেত।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"How would you distil a reasoning model?","a":"Generate long chain-of-thought solutions from a strong reasoning teacher, filter by correctness, fine-tune the student on them, and possibly follow with on-policy KD or RL.","bn":"Teacher-এর reasoning লেখা ছেঁকে student-কে শেখাও।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is TAID or DistiLLM-style adaptive KD?","a":"Methods that adapt the target or the loss during training (interpolating or skewing the KL) to reduce the capacity gap and instability.","bn":"Training-এর সময় target মানিয়ে নেওয়া।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is the difference between top-k logit KD and sampled-logit KD?","a":"Top-k keeps the k highest-probability tokens (biased toward the head); sampled-logit methods sample tokens from the teacher distribution so the estimate is unbiased with fewer tokens.","bn":"Top-k মাথার অংশ; sampled unbiased।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What would you log during a KD run?","a":"CE and KL separately, total loss, grad_norm, learning rate, validation metric, and sample generations.","bn":"CE, KL, grad_norm, validation আর নমুনা লেখা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why log CE and KL separately?","a":"The mixed loss can fall while one term gets worse; separate curves show which signal is driving training.","bn":"মিশ্র loss কমলেও একটা খারাপ হতে পারে।","level":"medium","trick":false}]},"qb-rag":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Chunking, embeddings, hybrid search, reranking, evaluation and failure modes of retrieval-augmented generation.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Chunking, embedding, hybrid search, reranking, evaluation আর RAG-এর ব্যর্থতার কারণ।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is RAG in one sentence?","a":"Retrieve relevant documents at query time and put them in the prompt so the model answers from them; an open-book exam.","bn":"প্রশ্নের সময় প্রাসঙ্গিক লেখা খুঁজে prompt-এ দেওয়া; open-book পরীক্ষা।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"When RAG, when fine-tuning, when distillation?","a":"RAG for facts that change or need citations; fine-tuning for style, format or skills; distillation to shrink a model or transfer behaviour. They combine: distil the behaviour, retrieve the facts.","bn":"তথ্যের জন্য RAG, আচরণের জন্য fine-tuning, ছোট করার জন্য distillation।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What are the main stages of a RAG pipeline?","a":"Ingest and chunk, embed and index, retrieve (and rerank), assemble context, generate, and evaluate.","bn":"Chunk, embed, retrieve, rerank, generate, evaluate।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How do you choose chunk size?","a":"Match the natural unit of the document and test several sizes on questions with known answers. Too small fragments the context; too big dilutes the embedding. Mine: 450 tokens with 100 overlap for statutes.","bn":"ডকুমেন্টের স্বাভাবিক একক ধরে, কয়েক size test করে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why use overlap between chunks?","a":"So a sentence or clause that straddles a boundary still appears whole in at least one chunk.","bn":"সীমানায় আটকে যাওয়া বাক্য যেন পুরো থাকে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What does an embedding model do?","a":"Maps text to a vector so that similar meanings are close, enabling semantic search.","bn":"লেখাকে vector বানায়, অর্থ কাছাকাছি হলে vector-ও কাছাকাছি।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why do e5 models need &quot;query:&quot; and &quot;passage:&quot; prefixes?","a":"They were trained with asymmetric prefixes; leaving them out doesn&#39;t error but silently lowers retrieval quality.","bn":"Prefix ছাড়া error আসে না, কিন্তু মান কমে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Bi-encoder vs cross-encoder?","a":"A bi-encoder embeds query and passage separately (fast, precomputable); a cross-encoder reads them together (more accurate, too slow for the whole corpus), so use it to rerank a short list.","bn":"Bi-encoder দ্রুত; cross-encoder নির্ভুল কিন্তু ধীর, তাই শুধু rerank-এ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why hybrid search?","a":"Dense retrieval captures meaning but blurs exact identifiers; BM25 catches exact terms but misses paraphrases. Mixing them covers both. Mine: 0.6 semantic + 0.4 BM25.","bn":"Dense অর্থ ধরে, BM25 নির্দিষ্ট শব্দ ধরে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is RRF?","a":"Reciprocal rank fusion merges ranked lists by summing 1/(k + rank) per list, with no score normalisation needed.","bn":"বিভিন্ন তালিকার র‍্যাঙ্ক যোগ করে মেলায়।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Explain BM25 briefly.","a":"Rare query terms count more (IDF), repeated terms saturate (k1), and long documents are penalised (b).","bn":"বিরল শব্দের মূল্য বেশি, পুনরাবৃত্তির সীমা, দৈর্ঘ্যের শাস্তি।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is a similarity threshold for?","a":"To avoid injecting irrelevant chunks when nothing in the corpus matches. Calibrate it on your data; e5 cosines cluster high, so a 0.40 cut-off may rarely trigger.","bn":"কিছু না মিললে অপ্রাসঙ্গিক chunk ঢোকানো ঠেকাতে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why top-3 chunks and not top-10?","a":"A small model&#39;s context is limited and extra chunks add noise; I found about three chunks (roughly 1,350 tokens) was the most my 2B model used well.","bn":"ছোট model বেশি context সামলাতে পারে না।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is multi-query expansion?","a":"Generate paraphrases of the user&#39;s question and merge the results, so one awkward phrasing doesn&#39;t miss the answer.","bn":"প্রশ্নের কয়েকটা রূপ বানিয়ে খোঁজা।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is HyDE?","a":"Have the model write a hypothetical answer and embed that instead of the question, because answers resemble passages more than questions do.","bn":"কাল্পনিক উত্তর বানিয়ে সেটার embedding দিয়ে খোঁজা।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What are the main RAG failure modes?","a":"Retrieval misses the answer, retrieves distractors, the context is cut or badly ordered, or the generator ignores or contradicts the context.","bn":"Retrieval ভুল, বাড়তি চেহারার অংশ, context কাটা, বা generator context অগ্রাহ্য করে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How do you evaluate retrieval separately from generation?","a":"With questions that have known source passages: recall@k, MRR, nDCG for retrieval; faithfulness and relevance for generation.","bn":"Known source সহ প্রশ্নে recall@k, MRR।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does faithfulness measure and how?","a":"Whether claims in the answer are supported by the context; measured by claim-level checking with an LLM or NLI model, ideally calibrated on human labels.","bn":"উত্তরের দাবি context-এ আছে কি না।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Can RAG remove hallucination?","a":"No; it reduces it. The model can still ignore the context or retrieve the wrong passage, so use abstention, citations and verification.","bn":"কমায়, পুরোপুরি দূর করে না।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"What is a vector database and what is an ANN index?","a":"A store for embeddings with fast nearest-neighbour search; ANN indexes (HNSW, IVF) trade a little recall for much speed.","bn":"Embedding রাখার database; ANN একটু recall দিয়ে গতি কেনে।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How big is an embedding index?","a":"Chunks × dimensions × bytes per number. Mine: 36,029 × 1,024 × 4 bytes ≈ 148 MB (141 MiB).","bn":"chunk × dimension × 4 byte।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How does RAG work offline on a phone?","a":"Ship a prebuilt index, run lexical search or a small on-device embedder, keep context short, and memory-map big files. My app used a Unicode-aware lexical scorer and a Kotlin + ONNX Runtime module.","bn":"আগে থেকে বানানো index ফোনে, ছোট context।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is contextual retrieval?","a":"Prepending a short document-level description to each chunk before embedding so chunks aren&#39;t ambiguous out of context.","bn":"Chunk-এর আগে তার প্রসঙ্গ জুড়ে দেওয়া।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What is GraphRAG?","a":"Building a knowledge graph from the corpus and retrieving over entities and relations, which helps global, multi-hop questions.","bn":"Graph বানিয়ে সম্পর্কের উপর খোঁজা।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Long-context model vs RAG?","a":"Long context avoids retrieval errors but costs more per query and degrades on very long inputs; RAG is cheaper, citable and scales to huge corpora. Often use both.","bn":"দীর্ঘ context খরচ বেশি; RAG সস্তা আর citation দেয়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is a prompt-injection risk in RAG?","a":"Retrieved documents can contain instructions that hijack the model. Treat retrieved text as data, filter it and limit the model&#39;s tools.","bn":"Retrieve করা লেখার ভেতরের নির্দেশ model-কে বিপথে নিতে পারে।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What makes multilingual RAG hard?","a":"Query and document languages differ, tokenisers handle scripts unevenly, and lexical search may ignore non-Latin scripts. Use a multilingual embedder and test with real queries.","bn":"ভাষা আলাদা, tokenizer অসম, lexical search অ-Latin বাদ দিতে পারে।","level":"medium","trick":false}]},"qb-education":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Tutoring behaviour, risks, Bangla constraints and evaluation for an education product.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Tutor-এর আচরণ, ঝুঁকি, Bangla-র সীমাবদ্ধতা আর education product-এর মূল্যায়ন।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"What makes a good AI tutor different from a good chatbot?","a":"It diagnoses the student&#39;s mistake, gives graded hints instead of the answer, and checks understanding. Frontier models often reveal answers too often.","bn":"ভুল ধরে, hint দেয়, বোঝা যাচ্ছে কি না দেখে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What did Bastani et al. find?","a":"In about 1,000 Turkish high-school students, plain GPT-4 raised practice scores but lowered unassisted exam scores by 17%; a guarded tutor with hints didn&#39;t.","bn":"সাধারণ GPT-4-এ practice ভালো, পরীক্ষায় 17% খারাপ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why distil for education?","a":"Per-student cost near zero on-device, children&#39;s data stays on the phone, offline use, and you can train pedagogy and Bangla into the model.","bn":"খরচ প্রায় শূন্য, privacy, offline, আর পড়ানোর ধরন শেখানো।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What&#39;s the size floor for a stand-alone tutor?","a":"In a 2026 study, models of 1.2B or fewer hallucinated in 94% of sessions; I&#39;d target 2–4B effective plus retrieval and a verifier.","bn":"১.২B-এর নিচে ব্যর্থ; 2–4B + retrieval + verifier।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why keep curriculum facts out of the weights?","a":"NCTB books change (three regimes in four years, 601 books revised for 2027), so facts belong in a versioned retrieval index.","bn":"বই বদলায়, তাই তথ্য index-এ।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How would you stop a tutor from leaking answers?","a":"Hint-level state in the dialogue manager, training data without leaking turns, and an output check against the stored solution; track leakage rate as a release metric.","bn":"Hint স্তরের state, leak-মুক্ত data, দেখানোর আগে যাচাই।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Which learner model would you use?","a":"BKT to start (four parameters per skill), DKT once there are logs; the LLM only reads a summary.","bn":"শুরুতে BKT, পরে DKT।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why not let the LLM do arithmetic?","a":"LLMs make arithmetic errors; Khanmigo&#39;s calculator-style math agent halved answer-giving and caught mistakes. Use a verifier tool.","bn":"হিসাব tool-কে দাও।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Biggest Bangla-specific problems?","a":"Token cost (Llama 3.1 about 8 tokens per word), uneven model quality in Bengali, mostly non-commercial datasets and no Bangla tutoring benchmark.","bn":"Token খরচ, মান, licence, benchmark-এর অভাব।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How would you evaluate a Bangla tutor?","a":"Leakage and correctness automatically, teacher rubric on a sample, BEnQA and BanglaMATH for knowledge, and a pilot with an unassisted post-test.","bn":"Leakage, শিক্ষকদের rubric, BEnQA, pilot।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What safety issues come with minors?","a":"Age-appropriate content, privacy and consent, no emotion recognition (banned in EU schools), human escalation for self-harm, and no off switch for guardrails.","bn":"বয়স-উপযোগী, privacy, মানুষের কাছে পাঠানো।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How does your thesis relate to education?","a":"Same constraints (small model, offline phone, Bangla users, grounded answers) and the same pipeline; the objective changes from answering to guiding.","bn":"সমস্যা একই, লক্ষ্য আলাদা।","level":"easy","trick":false}]},"qb-thesis":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Rapid-fire facts and defences about the Gemma-2 9B to 2B legal distillation project.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Gemma-2 9B থেকে 2B legal distillation project-এর দ্রুত তথ্য আর ব্যাখ্যা।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"Describe your thesis in two sentences.","a":"I built an offline Bangladeshi-law assistant that combines hybrid RAG with a Gemma-2 2B student distilled from a 9B teacher (SeqKD with top-50 logits), and I shipped it as a 1.6 GB model on an Android phone. Distillation roughly doubled ROUGE-L over the undistilled student.","bn":"RAG আর distilled 2B model দিয়ে offline আইন-সহায়ক, Android-এ 1.6 GB।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Teacher and student?","a":"Teacher <code>google/gemma-2-9b-it</code> (4-bit NF4), student <code>google/gemma-2-2b-it</code> (about 2.6B parameters with embeddings).","bn":"Teacher Gemma-2 9B, student Gemma-2 2B।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why a same-family pair?","a":"They share the SentencePiece tokenizer, so token ids match and KL over ids is meaningful. A 27B or 70B teacher wouldn&#39;t fit in my 16 GB VRAM either.","bn":"Tokenizer এক, তাই KL অর্থপূর্ণ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why was distillation offline?","a":"The 9B teacher (about 5–6 GB in 4-bit) and the 2B student with LoRA and optimiser (about 8–10 GB) together exceeded my 16 GB RTX 4080 Super. The cost is a fixed curriculum.","bn":"১৬ GB VRAM-এ দুটো একসাথে ধরে না।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What exactly did you store from the teacher?","a":"The generated text and, per generated token, the top-50 probabilities at T = 4.0 (about 95% of the mass), about 1.9 GB for 9,429 samples.","bn":"লেখা আর প্রতি token-এ top-50 probability (T = 4.0)।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Is your method standard KD or SeqKD?","a":"A hybrid: teacher-generated sequences (SeqKD) trained with CE, plus a KL term on the saved top-50 soft distributions.","bn":"SeqKD আর soft KL-এর মিশ্রণ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What was your training curriculum?","a":"Phase 1: CE only, 2 epochs, LR 1e-4. Phase 2: 0.6·CE + 0.4·KL, 2 epochs, LR 5e-5.","bn":"প্রথমে CE, তারপর 0.6·CE + 0.4·KL।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"LoRA settings?","a":"r = 32, α = 64, all seven projection modules, QLoRA with NF4 and double quantisation, AdamW, batch 1 × 16 accumulation, max sequence 2048, bf16.","bn":"r = 32, α = 64, সব 7 module।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Why did Approaches 1 and 2 fail?","a":"Plain CE on teacher answers (first final answers, then chain-of-thought) stalled at about 0.20 ROUGE-L; the breakthrough was adding soft targets in a sequence-level scheme with a curriculum.","bn":"শুধু CE-তে ~0.20-এ আটকে গিয়েছিল।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What were the final results?","a":"ROUGE-L 0.4715, BLEU 0.2551, BERTScore 0.5679, against the undistilled baseline&#39;s ROUGE-L 0.2323 and BERTScore 0.2340.","bn":"ROUGE-L 0.4715 (baseline 0.2323)।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What did the lawyer say?","a":"One practising lawyer rated 50 answers on usefulness, correctness and grounding: mean 4.16/5 (13 fives, 32 fours, 5 threes).","bn":"৫০টা উত্তরে গড় 4.16/5।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Limitations of a single lawyer rating?","a":"One rater means no agreement measure and possible bias, and only the final system was rated, so there&#39;s no baseline comparison.","bn":"একজন rater, তুলনা নেই।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Chunking choices?","a":"At most 450 tokens, 100 overlap, sentence-aware, giving 36,029 chunks; statutory provisions run 300–500 tokens. 256-token chunks scored worse.","bn":"≤450 token, 100 overlap, 36,029 chunk।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Embeddings?","a":"multilingual-e5-large, 1024-d, normalised, with query/passage prefixes; e5-small (384-d) only for the mobile benchmark.","bn":"multilingual-e5-large, 1024-d।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Retrieval design?","a":"Hybrid 0.6 semantic + 0.4 BM25, a 0.40 cosine gate with a fallback, top-10 candidates, top-3 to the model.","bn":"0.6/0.4 hybrid, 0.40 gate, top-3।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Where did the synthetic questions come from?","a":"gemma3:27b wrote about 3 questions per chunk (chunks of at least 30 words), deduplicated to 14,514.","bn":"gemma3:27b, প্রতি chunk-এ ~3টা, 14,514টা।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What did the quality gate do?","a":"Rejected teacher answers shorter than 80 characters or containing evasion phrases; 9,429 of 14,514 (65%) were kept.","bn":"৮০ অক্ষরের কম বা এড়িয়ে যাওয়া উত্তর বাদ।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about the frozen-adapter bug.","a":"r = 32 scored lower than r = 16 although the loss looked fine; grad_norm was 0.0 for 314 steps. <code>PeftModel.from_pretrained</code> defaults to non-trainable and I hadn&#39;t called <code>prepare_model_for_kbit_training</code>. After the fix grad_norm was 0.45–0.58.","bn":"grad_norm 314 step শূন্য ছিল।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about the prompt mismatch bug.","a":"Benchmark used a loose 4-line prompt while training used the strict 6-rule prompt, and the reference was the teacher&#39;s full reasoning rather than its final answer. Using the exact training prompt fixed it.","bn":"Benchmark-এর prompt আর training-এর prompt আলাদা ছিল।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about the logit/text misalignment.","a":"The text target was only the final answer (about 90 tokens) while the logits covered the full response (about 218 tokens), so CE and KL ran over different sequences. I stored the full response.","bn":"Text আর logit আলাদা অংশ কভার করছিল।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why KL weight 0.4?","a":"0.5 scored lower (ROUGE-L 0.4324 vs 0.4422, BERTScore 0.4930 vs 0.5343); CE should lead and KL support.","bn":"0.5-এ খারাপ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What did Phase 3 show?","a":"An extra KL-only phase lowered ROUGE-L from 0.4715 to 0.4397; without the CE anchor the student drifted on truncated distributions.","bn":"CE ছাড়া drift।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What does the 2×2 ablation show?","a":"ROUGE-L 0.099 (no distillation, no retrieval), 0.112 (distilled, no retrieval), 0.232 (retrieval, no distillation), 0.472 (both): both pieces are needed, and distillation without retrieval invents citations.","bn":"দুটোই দরকার।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How did you deploy to the phone?","a":"Merge the adapter into fp16 (about 4.5 GB), convert to GGUF f16 (5.23 GB), quantise to Q4_K_M (1.6 GB), run with llama.cpp in a React Native app with a Kotlin module.","bn":"Merge, GGUF, Q4_K_M, llama.cpp।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Phone performance?","a":"Pixel 6 (Android 16): 4–8 tokens/s, 15–40 s per answer, about 2 GB RAM, about 3 GB storage.","bn":"4–8 tokens/s, ~2 GB RAM।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How reliable are the mobile scores?","a":"They are PC-simulated with e5-small, a stand-in rather than the on-device pipeline: ROUGE-L 0.4639 vs 0.4715.","bn":"PC-তে অনুকরণ করা।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"What was your Bangla result?","a":"50 Bangla questions against the English corpus, answers in English: ROUGE-L 0.4083. I can&#39;t say how the questions were made, so the BERTScore (0.8133) isn&#39;t comparable with the English one.","bn":"ROUGE-L 0.4083; তুলনা করা যায় না।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"Weaknesses?","a":"Not legal advice, an unreliable bimodal LLM judge, 5 ambiguous test questions, fixed offline curriculum, English-only answers, one lawyer, and a small test set.","bn":"আইনি পরামর্শ না, judge অনির্ভরযোগ্য, ছোট test set।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What would you do differently today?","a":"Use on-policy KD (GKD or MiniLLM-style) against exposure bias, keep some abstentions in training, add confidence intervals and a Bangla set, and compare against a stronger same-family teacher.","bn":"On-policy KD, abstain উদাহরণ, confidence interval।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why is ROUGE-L your main metric?","a":"It rewards the right facts in the right order and tolerates paraphrase better than ROUGE-N, but it can&#39;t catch a wrong section number, so I added BERTScore and a lawyer.","bn":"ক্রম ধরে; কিন্তু ভুল সংখ্যা ধরে না।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why did your judge fail?","a":"Scores were bimodal (25 ones, 15 fives) and 15 answers with ROUGE-L above 0.50 got Faithfulness 1, so I relied on ROUGE-L, BERTScore and the lawyer.","bn":"নম্বর দুই প্রান্তে।","level":"hard","trick":false}]},"qb-mlops-responsible":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Bias, hallucination, privacy, licences, tracking, drift and deployment in short answers.</p>\n","bn":"<p>Bias, hallucination, privacy, licence, tracking, drift আর deployment ছোট উত্তরে।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"Why do LLMs hallucinate?","a":"They are trained to produce likely text, not true text; gaps in knowledge, ambiguous prompts and pressure to answer all yield fluent errors.","bn":"সম্ভাব্য লেখা বানায়, সত্য না।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Hallucination mitigations?","a":"Grounding with retrieval, abstention training, verifiers or tools, constrained outputs and citations.","bn":"Retrieval, abstain, verifier, citation।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What is PII and how do you protect it?","a":"Personally identifiable information; minimise collection, anonymise logs, encrypt storage and get consent.","bn":"ব্যক্তিগত তথ্য; কম নাও, anonymise, encrypt।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"Licences: Apache 2.0, MIT, Gemma Terms?","a":"Apache and MIT are permissive; Gemma 1–3 use custom Gemma Terms (derivatives inherit restrictions), while Gemma 4 is Apache 2.0. Always read the current terms.","bn":"Apache/MIT উদার; Gemma 1–3-এর নিজস্ব শর্ত।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What do you track in experiments?","a":"Code version, data version, config, seed, metrics and artefacts, with tools like W&amp;B or MLflow.","bn":"Code, data, config, seed, metric।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"How do you make a run reproducible?","a":"Fix seeds, pin library versions, version data and configs, and log hardware; some GPU ops stay nondeterministic.","bn":"Seed, version, data-config সংরক্ষণ।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"What is data drift?","a":"The live input distribution shifts away from the training distribution, such as a new curriculum or new slang; monitor inputs and quality.","bn":"Live input training থেকে সরে যায়।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How do you A/B test a model change?","a":"Randomly split users, pick the metric and sample size in advance, guard against harms, and look at confidence intervals before shipping.","bn":"এলোমেলো ভাগ, আগে metric ঠিক।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Canary vs shadow deployment?","a":"Canary sends a small share of real traffic to the new model; shadow runs it on live traffic without showing its output.","bn":"Canary অল্প traffic; shadow দেখায় না।","level":"hard","trick":false},{"q":"How do you estimate training cost?","a":"GPU-hours = FLOPs ÷ (sustained FLOP/s), with FLOPs ≈ 6·N·D, times price per GPU-hour, plus data generation and evaluation.","bn":"6·N·D ÷ sustained FLOP/s × দাম।","level":"medium","trick":false}]},"qb-trick":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Questions designed to catch common confusions; each answer names the trap.</p>\n","bn":"<p>সাধারণ গোলমাল ধরার জন্য বানানো প্রশ্ন; প্রতিটা উত্তরে ফাঁদের নাম আছে।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"Is distillation temperature the same as sampling temperature?","a":"No. Distillation T softens distributions inside the training loss; sampling T controls randomness at inference. The student is deployed at T = 1.","bn":"না, একটা training-এর loss-এর ভেতরে, অন্যটা inference-এ।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Is RAG a kind of distillation?","a":"No. RAG supplies knowledge at inference through retrieval; distillation trains a smaller model. One changes the input, the other the weights.","bn":"না; RAG input বদলায়, distillation weight।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Is LoRA the same as quantisation?","a":"No. LoRA adds a small trainable low-rank update; quantisation lowers precision of weights. QLoRA combines them.","bn":"না; LoRA ছোট adapter, quantisation precision কমানো।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Does QLoRA quantise the adapters?","a":"No, only the frozen base weights (4-bit NF4); adapters are trained in 16-bit.","bn":"না, শুধু base।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Does a higher temperature change the most likely token?","a":"No. Dividing by a positive T keeps the logit order, so only the probabilities change.","bn":"না, ক্রম একই থাকে।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Is forward KL(p ‖ q) the same as KL(q ‖ p)?","a":"No. KL is asymmetric, and the direction decides mean-seeking versus mode-seeking behaviour.","bn":"না, অসম।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Perplexity of 1 means what?","a":"A perfectly confident correct model; it is the lowest possible value. A uniform guess over V tokens has perplexity V.","bn":"সবচেয়ে ভালো।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"BLEU 0.25 is bad, right?","a":"Not necessarily. BLEU is precision-based for translation; for long free-form answers with terse references it is naturally low while ROUGE-L can be high.","bn":"না; লম্বা উত্তরে BLEU স্বভাবতই কম।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Higher BERTScore means the answer is more correct?","a":"Not always. It measures embedding similarity, which can stay high when one key fact (a section number) is wrong, and its scale depends on whether baseline rescaling is used.","bn":"না; একটা ভুল তথ্যেও বেশি থাকতে পারে।","level":"hard","trick":true},{"q":"Does a falling training loss prove the model is learning?","a":"No. A frozen adapter or misaligned targets can show a smooth loss. Check grad_norm and held-out metrics.","bn":"না।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Can you merge LoRA into an already-quantised model?","a":"Not cleanly; merge into the 16-bit base first, then quantise.","bn":"না; আগে merge।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Accuracy 99% means the classifier is good?","a":"Not on imbalanced data; all-negative can score 99%.","bn":"না।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Is a bigger teacher always better?","a":"No. Beyond a gap in capacity the student can&#39;t follow it; a medium teacher or an assistant can give better students.","bn":"না; ফাঁক বড় হলে শেখে না।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Does top-50 logit storage mean you stored the whole distribution?","a":"No; about 95% of the mass in my case, so the tail is ignored and the target is slightly biased even after renormalising.","bn":"না।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Is the teacher trained during standard KD?","a":"No, it&#39;s frozen.","bn":"না।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Can you use a closed API model as a distillation teacher?","a":"Technically yes (text outputs), but many terms forbid training competing models, and you get at most top-20 logprobs. Check the terms; prefer open teachers.","bn":"কারিগরি ভাবে হ্যাঁ, কিন্তু শর্ত দেখো।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Does RAG remove the need to fine-tune?","a":"No. Retrieval gives facts, not skills or style; a small model may still need distillation to use context well.","bn":"না।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Is cosine similarity a distance metric?","a":"No; cosine distance (1 − cosine) can break the triangle inequality.","bn":"না।","level":"hard","trick":true},{"q":"Does a cross-entropy of 0.5 mean 50% accuracy?","a":"No. CE is the average negative log-probability of the true class; it isn&#39;t a percentage.","bn":"না।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Does more data always help distillation?","a":"No. Low-quality or off-distribution teacher outputs can hurt, and my extra KL-only phase lowered scores. Quality gates matter.","bn":"না।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Is a smaller model always faster on a phone?","a":"Mostly, since decoding is memory-bandwidth bound, but the runtime, quantisation kernels and long prompts (prefill) change that.","bn":"সাধারণত, কিন্তু runtime আর prompt-এর দৈর্ঘ্য প্রভাব ফেলে।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"LLM judge says 5/5. Is the answer correct?","a":"Not necessarily; judges are biased and may be insensitive to factual errors, so check against humans.","bn":"না।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Does int8 quantisation halve the model compared with fp16?","a":"Weights only: 1 byte versus 2 per parameter, so yes, but the KV cache and activations are separate.","bn":"Weight-এর ক্ষেত্রে হ্যাঁ।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Does LoRA with larger rank always give better results?","a":"No. Mine at r = 32 outperformed r = 16 only after fixing a bug, and higher r also costs more; returns diminish.","bn":"না।","level":"medium","trick":true},{"q":"Can a student trained on teacher text inherit the teacher&#39;s mistakes?","a":"Yes. SeqKD copies errors too, which is why you filter teacher outputs and add verification.","bn":"হ্যাঁ।","level":"easy","trick":true},{"q":"Does a 2B model fit on any phone?","a":"Only when quantised: 2.6B × 5.21 bits ≈ 1.7 GB for weights, plus KV cache and app, so about 2 GB of RAM in my test; low-end phones may not cope.","bn":"Quantise করলে; কম RAM-এর ফোনে নয়।","level":"medium","trick":true}]},"qb-behavioral":{"blocks":[{"key":"oneline","en":"<p>Short STAR answers built only from my real project story.</p>\n","bn":"<p>আমার আসল project-এর গল্প থেকে বানানো ছোট STAR উত্তর।</p>\n"},{"key":"questions"}],"questions":[{"q":"Tell me about a time something silently failed.","a":"In my distillation run the loss looked normal but r = 32 scored lower than r = 16. I logged grad_norm, found it was 0.0 for 314 steps because the adapter was frozen, fixed the loading order and the next run trained (grad_norm 0.45–0.58). Lesson: log gradient norms.","bn":"loss ঠিক ছিল, কিন্তু grad_norm শূন্য; কারণ খুঁজে ঠিক করেছি।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about a hard constraint you worked around.","a":"My 16 GB GPU couldn&#39;t hold the 9B teacher and the 2B student together, so I generated the teacher&#39;s answers and top-50 probabilities offline and trained from files, accepting a fixed curriculum.","bn":"১৬ GB-এ দুটো ধরে না, তাই teacher-এর output আগে save করেছি।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about a time your first approach failed.","a":"Two approaches that copied teacher text with plain cross-entropy stalled at about 0.20 ROUGE-L. I switched to sequence-level distillation with soft targets and a two-phase curriculum and reached 0.4715.","bn":"দুটো পদ্ধতি আটকে গিয়েছিল; soft target আর curriculum-এ পথ পেলাম।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about a mistake you caught in your own evaluation.","a":"My benchmark prompt differed from the training prompt and the reference was the teacher&#39;s full reasoning. I aligned them and compared final answer to final answer.","bn":"Benchmark-এর prompt আলাদা ছিল; মিলিয়ে ঠিক করলাম।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about a time you had to be honest about limitations.","a":"I reported that my LLM judge was bimodal and that my mobile scores were PC-simulated, and relied on a lawyer rating and ROUGE-L instead.","bn":"Judge-এর সীমা আর mobile score-এর সীমা খোলাখুলি বলেছি।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Tell me about a time you learned something new fast.","a":"I learned llama.cpp, GGUF conversion and Android native modules for deployment; a missing <code>tokenizer.model</code> broke conversion and a 141 MB matrix crashed the JS heap, and I fixed both.","bn":"GGUF আর Android native module শিখেছি।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"Why this role?","a":"I like making models small and useful, and my project already tied distillation, retrieval and phone deployment together. Education adds a goal I care about: teaching in Bangla on cheap phones.","bn":"ছোট কিন্তু কাজের model বানাতে ভালো লাগে।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What would you do in your first 30 days?","a":"Learn the data and eval setup, reproduce a baseline, build a leakage and correctness eval, then try one improvement with an ablation and report honestly.","bn":"আগে eval আর baseline।","level":"medium","trick":false},{"q":"How do you handle not knowing an answer?","a":"Say so, reason aloud from first principles, state what I&#39;d check, and offer what I did in my project if relevant.","bn":"না জানলে বলো, ভেবে দেখাও।","level":"easy","trick":false},{"q":"What questions do you have for us?","a":"What does the student model need to do that the teacher can&#39;t? How do you evaluate tutoring quality? What&#39;s the plan for Bangla data and licences?","bn":"Student-কে কী করতে হবে, মূল্যায়ন কীভাবে, Bangla data-র licence।","level":"easy","trick":false}]}});
